                                      "content": "Java heap ceiling (-Xmx, e.g. 2G, 3072M). Leave empty to size it automatically to 75% of the container memory limit — it then tracks the limit whenever you resize the server. If you set it yourself, keep roughly 25% below the limit: the JVM needs headroom for non-heap memory, and exceeding the limit gets the server OOM-killed.",
